        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(durable): wire agent session runtime coordination",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThis PR wires the durable runtime foundation from PR2 into agent/session/subagent paths so OpenClaw can record durable context for chat sends, agent runs, subagent child runs, parent fan-in, yield progress, and restart/recovery inspection.\n\nThe target behavior is: parent agents should have durable child/fan-in state; one failed child should not make sibling completion invisible; and Gateway/session restart should leave inspectable runtime state instead of silent coordinator ambiguity.\n\n## Dependency Chain\n\nThis is PR3 in the replacement durable runtime stack:\n\n1. PR1: durable session/task runtime RFC v2.\n2. PR2: durable runtime foundation.\n3. PR3: agent/session/subagent wiring, this PR.\n\nThis branch is stacked on the refreshed PR2 branch. The upstream PR diff against `main` is cumulative. For delta-only review after PR2, use:\n\nhttps://github.com/mjnkao/openclaw/compare/codex/openclaw-durable-runtime-foundation-v2-ready...codex/openclaw-durable-runtime-agent-v2-ready\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds:\n\n- Gateway `chat.send` and `agent.run` durable context refs;\n- user-turn transcript durable context propagation;\n- embedded-agent yield progress for resumable parent turns;\n- subagent child-run mirroring and parent fan-in association;\n- task completion contract metadata for durable parent/child lifecycle;\n- status-notice display metadata for durable/yield progress;\n- protocol schema fields for durable context references.\n\n## Explicit Non-Scope\n\n- Work module.\n- Workboard UI/tools.\n- Task Flow projection adapters.\n- Retention/compaction.\n- Postgres/multi-worker lease contention.\n- Durable write controls such as cancel/retry/resume/signal.\n\n## Latest Reviewer Follow-Up\n\nUpdated on 2026-07-02 after rebasing onto the refreshed PR2 foundation branch.\n\nHead: `21d43fd9c4a04c6b2da11fc05125940ce4ca652e`.\n\nAddressed ClawSweeper P2 finding:\n\n- Oversized chat-history placeholders now preserve `__openclaw.idempotencyKey` along with `id` and `seq`, keeping existing client correlation/dedupe metadata intact.\n- The branch no longer carries the superseded PR2 foundation commits; it is stacked on the refreshed PR2 head.\n\nRegression coverage added:\n\n- `src/gateway/server-methods/chat-history-omission-logging.test.ts` verifies direct oversized replacement preserves `idempotencyKey: \"oversized-key\"`.\n- `src/gateway/session-utils.fs.test.ts` was rerun in the same proof shard and kept the existing oversized transcript metadata assertion green.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPost-rebase validation:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/chat-history-omission-logging.test.ts src/gateway/session-utils.fs.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods/chat.directive-tags.test.ts`\n  - 7 files, 549 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/generate-docs-map.mjs --check`\n  - passed with `docs/docs_map.md is up to date`.\n- `git diff --check origin/main HEAD`\n  - passed.\n\nEarlier focused validation remains recorded in `docs/specs/durable-runtime-agent-session-pr-proof-2026-07-01.md`, including:\n\n- Gateway/context/server-methods shard: 6 files, 176 tests passed;\n- agent tools shard: 2 files, 67 tests passed;\n- durable fan-in/subagent/agent-turn shard: 3 files, 14 tests passed;\n- Gateway durable matrix: 2 files, 4 tests passed;\n- Kysely verify and guardrails checks passed;\n- `npm run tsgo:core`, `npm run tsgo:core:test`, and `npm run tsgo:prod` passed on the stacked branch.\n\n## Local Build Note\n\n`env CI=true npm run build` was attempted locally. Dependency installation and bundled plugin assets completed, then the root `tsdown` build emitted only heartbeat lines for more than ten minutes and was manually interrupted. This is not recorded as passing build proof; CI or a maintainer machine should still run the full build before merge.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis PR replaces the agent/session/subagent wiring portion of #97508 with runtime-oriented naming and a narrower dependency chain.\n",
        "branch": "codex/openclaw-durable-runtime-agent-v2-ready",
